<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17842" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">făvus</span></b> , i, m.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a honey-comb.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">favus est, quem fingunt (apes) multicavatum e
					cera, cum singula cava sena latera habeant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 16, 24</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cic. Off. 1, 44, 157</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 11,
				2, 57</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 1, 344</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4,
			161</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 8, 678</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. F. 4,
				152</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mellis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					1 Reg. 14, 27</span></i>
			 et saep.—Prov.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Crescere tamquam favum,</span>”
				i. e. <i>imperceptibly</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 43</span></i>
			 and 76.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a hexagonal stone
				in a pavement</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 7, 1</span></i>.</div>
